Project limits on the built contracts, run in the embedded provider's runtime (pallet-contracts 51, 1 MiB of contract memory).
Each PROBE line is printed by a temporary provider test. It sets a Project up through the provider (two or more workers, one
proposal with one milestone, planning accepted and, in the 'approved' runs, the approval), restores the stored state and calls
the Project directly with the provider's execution gas (128 MiB of proof). Every task has the stated number of assignees.
create_task is kept. At each step the other messages are run and rolled back: view, set_task_assignees, delete_task (draft
runs) and then approve_execution (draft runs), submit_milestone, accept_milestone and evaluate_project one after the other;
the chain stops at the first that fails. 'create_task with N tasks held' is the first create_task that failed.
An ordinary Kreivo transaction gets 2,446,677 bytes of proof.
The 'bounds' lines create tasks with 24 assignees, of which sixteen encode to 12,369 bytes, and proposals of ten milestones.

